--- body ---

## Context

The locked Phase B dialogue policy (ticket 0214; Annex C) ships
three reply strings: ENCOURAGE, VERIFY, TERMINAL. The current
VERIFY string asks the agent to "verify and polish in ONE focused
pass", prioritising four §2 axes (per-row provenance, coverage,
temporality, internal consistency) — but invites the agent to do
this monolithically.

Author direction (2026-05-21): boost the verify round by *asking
the agent itself* to spin a panel of four axis-specialised verifier
subagents — one per §2 dimension, ideally on different models from
the subject agent where the platform supports cross-model handoff.
Monolithic introspection → distributed pluralistic review.

This is a v1 → v2 policy bump. The state-machine structure is
unchanged (VERIFY is still one slot, fired once per session); only
the VERIFY string content changes.

## Actions

1. Update `VERIFY_REPLY` in
   `experiments/sota/exp2_interactive_smoke.py` to the v2 wording
   (see PR for verbatim text).
2. Update unit test `test_three_reply_slot_constants_distinct` if
   the four-axis-marker check is too brittle — the v2 text uses
   uppercase axis names (ACCURACY/COHERENCE/PROVENANCE/TEMPORALITY)
   instead of lowercase markers; either keep both forms or relax to
   case-insensitive.
3. Bump the policy version reference in Annex C
   (`slides/manuscript/main.md`, *Phase B dialogue policy*) and
   inline the new VERIFY text verbatim (preserving the "fixed
   condition" framing).
4. Re-smoke Mistral end-to-end. Compare outcomes vs the v1 polished
   inventory: turn count, citations gained on the verify turn,
   whether the agent explicitly references "verifier subagents" in
   its response, source-cell quality.

## Tests

- `test_three_reply_slot_constants_distinct` (existing) — relaxed
  axis-marker check (case-insensitive).
- The state-machine end-to-end tests must continue to pass
  unchanged (they don't inspect VERIFY content beyond presence).

## Out of scope

- Tooling the agent's subagent dispatch (we cannot force it; the
  prompt is a *suggestion*).
- Changing the ENCOURAGE or TERMINAL strings.
- Per-axis verdict aggregation (the agent integrates internally;
  we only see the final polished inventory).

## Exit criteria

- [ ] VERIFY_REPLY updated to v2 wording.
- [ ] Annex C carries the v2 text verbatim with a version note.
- [ ] Unit tests green.
- [ ] One re-smoke artefact on Mistral committed; turn-by-turn
      cost/classification recorded; qualitative comparison with the
      v1 polished inventory documented in the smoke commit message.
